<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pohansko</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pohansko is the site of a large ninth-century Great Moravian stronghold near Břeclav in South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a>. Excavations have revealed a fortified area with a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a>'s court, a stone church surrounded by burials and extensive craft workshops, making it one of the key sites for the Slavic state of Great Moravia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pohansko.jpg" alt="Pohansko" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pudelek (Marcin Szala) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:B%C5%99eclav_(Lundenburg)_castle.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
